{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/matching/reader-brief-run.md clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/matching/MATCHING-v2.md clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/matching/ruler-questions.json docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/questions-v1.json clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/matching/opened-p2.json'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/matching/reader-brief-run.md clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/matching/MATCHING-v2.md clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/matching/ruler-questions.json docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/questions-v1.json clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/matching/opened-p2.json'","aggregated_output":"# Question identity reading for a measured run (read-only)\n\nYou decide, for each question a system opened by itself in one run, whether it is the same question as one of 23 reference questions.\n\n**Files** (in `clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/matching/`):\n- `opened-p<N>.json`: the run's opened questions (run, id, the item where opened, description, outcome, period). N is the run\n  number given below.\n- `ruler-questions.json`: the 23 reference questions. Read each one's full entry in\n  `docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/questions-v1.json` when deciding.\n\n**The rule.** Apply MATCHING-v2.md §1, read in full.\n- An opened question is the same as a reference question when the same reported figure or event settles both.\n- Three kinds of extra wording do not separate them:\n  - a part, programme or single deal of a reference total;\n  - the same event under another deadline;\n  - a later milestone, variant or parenthetical widening that the question's own check does not rest on.\n- An amount held at a different date is not the same.\n- A yes/no signing question beside an amount question stays apart.\n- Extra scope that is its own check and could resolve on its own stays apart.\n\n**For every opened question, write one line of JSON:**\n\n{\"run\": ..., \"id\": ..., \"match\": \"q05\" or \"none\", \"relation\": \"same\" | \"broader\" | \"narrower\" | \"overlapping\" | \"unrelated\", \"reason\": \"<one sentence>\"}\n\nJudge from the texts alone; do not consider how either question would be scored. Output only the JSON lines.\n# Unseeded measurement: matching rule, graded subset and predictions, version 2 (2026-11-10, D394)\n\nThis replaces MATCHING.md, which is kept. The council (`council/ga-codex.md`) asked for three changes, all made here: the seven are a\nsubset, not the product's set; dev-d1 clean-1 is NOT SAME; and every outcome has a defined verdict.\n\n## 1. The matching rule (an addition to the measurement; no frozen file changes)\n\nAn opened question is the same as a ruler question when the same reported figure or event settles both (D248 and its boundaries).\n**Extra wording that does not separate them:**\n- a part, programme or single deal of a reference total (D248 boundary 1; R2-e);\n- the same event under another deadline, in either direction (boundary 2);\n- a later milestone, variant or parenthetical widening that the question's own check does not rest on (boundary 3; R2-f for steps of\n  one approval process).\n\n**It stays apart only when:**\n- it is a yes/no signing question beside an amount question (the Ohio exception, D248); or\n- its extra scope is its own check and could resolve on its own, as a separately watched bet.\n\n**How the rule was set** (`reader-brief.md`):\n- Two blind readers, Codex and Claude, read the 28 questions opened by the three stored unseeded c8 dev runs.\n- They agreed on SAME or not SAME for 24 of 28.\n- A third reader decided the 4 disagreements against the full texts and the decisions: all SAME (`adjudication.md`). The rule above is\n  that reader's general statement.\n- **Limit:** boundary 2 (another deadline) applies to an event's date, not to an amount held at a date. dev-d1 clean-1 asks for credit\n  support at end-2027, while q09 asks for a broader total at FY2027 year-end. The amounts can differ, so it is NOT SAME, as both readers\n  had it. dev-d2 and dev-d3 clean-1 are checked in the same FY2027 10-K and stay SAME.\n\n**Mapping of the stored dev runs** (SAME only):\n\n| run | ruler questions opened as SAME |\n|---|---|\n| dev-d1 | q07, q08, q13, q18 |\n| dev-d2 | q07, q08, q09, q13, q18 |\n| dev-d3 | q05, q07, q08, q09, q18 (its hyperscaler question bundles 2026 and 2027: broader than q04 and q13) |\n\n## 2. The graded subset, and every other question reported\n\n`questions-v1.json` records, per question, the frozen gold's must-open entries it covers. Seven questions cover at least one: q04, q05,\nq08, q09, q13, q18 and q23.\n- **The graded subset.** These seven are the graded subset of this exploratory comparison: questions the frozen question gold says the\n  product must open.\n- **What the subset is not.** It is not the product's whole question set. An empty field means no must-open entry was written for that\n  question, not that the product must not open it. q07 is opened in every c8 run and has gold may-open entries.\n- **The other 16 are reported question by question.** For each: opened as SAME or not, and if judged, agree or disagree. None is called\n  \"by design\" except the company-figure questions (q01, q02, q03, q10, q11, q12, q19, q20, q22), which Alex's 2026-11-08 \"我觉得财务类型不应该是\n  thesis，而更多的是条件…\" and D370 keep out of opening. The rest (q06, q07, q14, q15, q16, q17, q21) are reported plainly.\n\n## 3. Predictions for an unseeded clean run (243 items, three draws), frozen\n\n| question | opened as SAME | agrees when opened |\n|---|---|---|\n| q08, q09, q13, q18 | in at least 2 of 3 draws each | in at least 2 of 3 draws each |\n| q05 | at most 2 of 3 | yes |\n| q04 | at most 1 of 3 (bundled with 2027) | yes |\n| q23 | at most 1 of 3 (opened in 1 of 3 seeded Stage 2 draws) | yes |\n\n- **Outcomes**, per question and draw: agree; disagree; not opened; opened but never judged; or run failed. Only \"agree\" counts.\n- **Stops**, each reported with its cost:\n  - a network cut in Step 1 is continued from the last completed article (`continue_clean_draw.py`);\n  - a judging stopped by the frozen judge's refusal is redone from its start;\n  - any other stop ends that draw;\n  - if three complete draws cannot be had, the measurement stops and goes to Alex.\n- **What a mapped view answers.** A mapped view carries the ruler question's text and ladder. Where the opened question has another\n  deadline, the report says that the judge answered the ruler's question, by its deadline, not the product's own question.\n- **Predicted subset agreements:** 4–5 of 7 per draw.\n- **The seeded clean arm of Stage 2 on the same seven:** 19 of 21, about 6.3 of 7 per draw.\n- **The observed gap** is the seeded subset agreements per draw on average, less the unseeded subset agreements per draw on average.\n  It is reported with the questions it falls on and their outcomes (not opened, or opened and disagreeing). The gap describes what the\n  unseeded system loses; it does not on its own say why. The gap mixes opening, evidence delivery and judging.\n- **Labels:**\n  - exploratory, from three dev runs;\n  - the seeded comparison was sent on another day, so the loss mixes opening with day-to-day sampling (a same-day seeded control would\n    cost about $7 more);\n  - three draws.\n\n## 4. What a paid run needs first (none of it built yet)\n\n- **The adapter extension.** All 22 seed views plus q23 are created with their ruler text and ladder, so the frozen scorer accepts the\n  run. Each clean thesis mapped SAME by the rule above, as applied by an independent reader to the run's opened questions before any\n  judging, feeds its links to that view. Unmapped ruler questions have no evidence and are not judged.\n- **A council read and tests with mutants.**\n- **Cost:** about $7–8 (three clean draws at about $2.3; no new control, since the seeded Stage 2 is the comparison).\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"q01\",\n  \"question\": \"What will Nvidia's total revenue be in FY2027?\",\n  \"unit\": \"USD\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q02\",\n  \"question\": \"What Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\",\n  \"unit\": \"USD\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q03\",\n  \"question\": \"What non-GAAP gross margin will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\",\n  \"unit\": \"percent (75 means 75%)\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q04\",\n  \"question\": \"How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026?\",\n  \"unit\": \"USD\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-12-31\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q05\",\n  \"question\": \"How will server DRAM and HBM contract prices in calendar 2027 compare with calendar 2026?\",\n  \"unit\": \"percent change 2027 vs 2026 (10 means up 10%)\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2028-01-31\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q06\",\n  \"question\": \"What share of calendar-2026 data-center AI accelerator spending will NVIDIA hold, by the first published full-year estimate?\",\n  \"unit\": \"percent\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q07\",\n  \"question\": \"Will Nvidia begin shipping its Rubin generation by December 31, 2026?\",\n  \"unit\": \"yes/no\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q08\",\n  \"question\": \"Will Chinese authorities issue any authorization for Chinese companies to import Nvidia H200 chips by January 31, 2027?\",\n  \"unit\": \"yes/no\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q09\",\n  \"question\": \"What total amount of financing commitments and capacity backstops to customers and partners will NVIDIA report outstanding at its FY2027 year-end?\",\n  \"unit\": \"USD\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q10\",\n  \"question\": \"What non-GAAP operating margin will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\",\n  \"unit\": \"percent\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q11\",\n  \"question\": \"What non-GAAP diluted earnings per share will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\",\n  \"unit\": \"USD per share\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q12\",\n  \"question\": \"How much will NVIDIA spend on capital expenditures in FY2027?\",\n  \"unit\": \"USD\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q13\",\n  \"question\": \"How much will the largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\",\n  \"unit\": \"USD\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2028-12-31\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q14\",\n  \"question\": \"What CoWoS advanced-packaging capacity will TSMC reach by the end of calendar 2026, in wafers a month?\",\n  \"unit\": \"wafers per month\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q15\",\n  \"question\": \"By how much will worldwide semiconductor industry revenue grow in calendar 2026 over 2025?\",\n  \"unit\": \"percent growth 2026 vs 2025\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q16\",\n  \"question\": \"How much will cloud providers spend on custom AI silicon (ASICs) in calendar 2026?\",\n  \"unit\": \"USD\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q17\",\n  \"question\": \"What share of China's calendar-2026 data-center AI accelerator spending will NVIDIA hold, by the first published full-year estimate?\",\n  \"unit\": \"percent\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q18\",\n  \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA begin shipping its Rubin Ultra generation, in Kyber NVL144 racks, by December 31, 2027?\",\n  \"unit\": \"yes/no\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-12-31\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q19\",\n  \"question\": \"How much revenue will NVIDIA report from standalone Vera CPUs in FY2027?\",\n  \"unit\": \"USD\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q20\",\n  \"question\": \"How much revenue will NVIDIA report from Blackwell and Rubin products in FY2027?\",\n  \"unit\": \"USD\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q21\",\n  \"question\": \"Will the SK Telecom AI factory built with NVIDIA GPUs begin operating by June 30, 2027?\",\n  \"unit\": \"yes/no\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-06-30\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q22\",\n  \"question\": \"What will Nvidia's total revenue be in FY2028?\",\n  \"unit\": \"USD\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2028-02-28\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"q23\",\n  \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA sign a guarantee of OpenAI's Ohio data-center lease by 2027-06-30?\",\n  \"unit\": \"yes/no\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-06-30\"\n }\n]{\n \"ruler_version\": 1,\n \"about\": \"22 seed questions (poc/seeds/nvda-2026-07-01-v2.json) + the one must_open bet no seed covers; must_open gists mapped by bet (D248)\",\n \"seeds_sha256\": \"fca16f42dd7153e852c42527883552b86567f33d7e1ed3c11ef600c8a37037d6\",\n \"gold_sha256\": \"6f9476bb6a81ea590af273a71565e7c3c0f49908d26274b8482d52cfdee31a21\",\n \"questions\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"q01\",\n   \"seed_view_id\": \"v1\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\",\n   \"question\": \"What will Nvidia's total revenue be in FY2027?\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\",\n   \"unit\": \"USD\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $500 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 500000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $400 billion and below $500 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 400000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 500000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $350 billion and below $400 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 350000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 400000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is at least $300 billion and below $350 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 300000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 350000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 total revenue is below $300 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": 300000000000.0\n    }\n   ],\n   \"covers_must_open\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"q02\",\n   \"seed_view_id\": \"v2\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\",\n   \"question\": \"What Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\",\n   \"unit\": \"USD\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 Data Center revenue is at least $440 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 440000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"at least $360 billion and below $440 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 360000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 440000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n     \"condition\": \"at least $310 billion and below $360 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 310000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 360000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"at least $260 billion and below $310 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 260000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 310000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"below $260 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": 260000000000.0\n    }\n   ],\n   \"covers_must_open\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"q03\",\n   \"seed_view_id\": \"v3\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\",\n   \"question\": \"What non-GAAP gross margin will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\",\n   \"unit\": \"percent (75 means 75%)\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 non-GAAP gross margin is at least 77%.\",\n     \"lo\": 77.0,\n     \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 non-GAAP gross margin is at least 75% but below 77%.\",\n     \"lo\": 75.0,\n     \"hi\": 77.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 non-GAAP gross margin is at least 73% but below 75%, compared with the article's 75% reference level.\",\n     \"lo\": 73.0,\n     \"hi\": 75.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 non-GAAP gross margin is at least 71% but below 73%.\",\n     \"lo\": 71.0,\n     \"hi\": 73.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2027 non-GAAP gross margin is below 71%.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": 71.0\n    }\n   ],\n   \"covers_must_open\": []\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"q04\",\n   \"seed_view_id\": \"v4\",\n   \"kind\": \"theme\",\n   \"question\": \"How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026?\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-12-31\",\n   \"unit\": \"USD\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Below $550 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is less than $550 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": 550000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$550 billion to below $600 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $550 billion and less than $600 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 550000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 600000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$600 billion to below $700 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $600 billion and less than $700 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 600000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 700000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$700 billion to below $800 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $700 billion and less than $800 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 700000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 800000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$800 billion or more\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $800 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 800000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": null\n    }\n   ],\n   \"covers_must_open\": [\n    {\n     \"day\": \"2026-07-07\",\n     \"input_id\": \"gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e\",\n     \"gist\": \"Combined calendar-2026 data-center capital expenditure of the 'big four' AI hyperscalers: five rungs around the ~$650bn plan (e.g. below $600bn / $600-640bn / $640-680bn / $680-750bn / above $750bn); due when the last of the four publishes calendar-2026 capex\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"day\": \"2026-07-07\",\n     \"input_id\": \"gnews:f8191f5bb960d79e47c73d6c\",\n     \"gist\": \"Combined calendar-2026 data-center capital expenditure of the 'big four' AI hyperscalers: five rungs around the ~$650bn plan (e.g. below $600bn / $600-640bn / $640-680bn / $680-750bn / above $750bn); due when the last of the four publishes calendar-2026 capex\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"q05\",\n   \"seed_view_id\": \"v5\",\n   \"kind\": \"theme\",\n   \"question\": \"How will server DRAM and HBM contract prices in calendar 2027 compare with calendar 2026?\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2028-01-31\",\n   \"unit\": \"percent change 2027 vs 2026 (10 means up 10%)\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Up 30% or more\",\n     \"condition\": \"2027 average contract prices at least 30% above 2026.\",\n     \"lo\": 30,\n     \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Up 10% to 30%\",\n     \"condition\": \"at least 10% and below 30% above 2026.\",\n     \"lo\": 10,\n     \"hi\": 30\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Flat\",\n     \"condition\": \"within 10% of 2026 either way.\",\n     \"lo\": -10,\n     \"hi\": 10\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Down 10% to 30%\",\n     \"condition\": \"at least 10% and below 30% under 2026.\",\n     \"lo\": -30,\n     \"hi\": -10\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Down 30% or more\",\n     \"condition\": \"30% or more under 2026.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": -30\n    }\n   ],\n   \"covers_must_open\": [\n    {\n     \"day\": \"2026-07-07\",\n     \"input_id\": \"gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e\",\n     \"gist\": \"Change in DRAM (including HBM) contract prices in calendar 2027 versus calendar 2026: five rungs (falls / flat within ±5% / rises 5-20% / rises 20-50% / rises more than 50%)\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"q06\",\n   \"seed_view_id\": \"v6\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\",\n   \"question\": \"What share of calendar-2026 data-center AI accelerator spending will NVIDIA hold, by the first published full-year estimate?\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\",\n   \"unit\": \"percent\",\n   \"